## Summary

Returning `$.response[status]` directly (without calling `.json()`, `.text()`, etc.) caused a spurious TypeScript type error for routes where the spec defines no response body.

`GenericResponseBuilder` uses `OmitValueWhenNever<Response>` to detect a "complete" response (nothing left to provide). The generator always emits `examples: {}` in the response type even when no named examples exist. This caused:

- `OmitValueWhenNever<{ content: never; headers: never; requiredHeaders: never; examples: {} }>` → `{ examples: {} }` (not omitted, since `{}` ≠ `never`)
- `object extends { examples: {} }` → `false`
- Type resolved to `GenericResponseBuilderInner` (with only `cookie` accessible), not `COUNTERFACT_RESPONSE`

So code like this incorrectly produced a type error:

```ts
export const DELETE: deleteOrder = ($) => {
  const deleted = $.context.deleteOrder($.path.orderId);
  if (!deleted) return $.response[404]; // ← type error (wrongly)
  return $.response[200];              // ← type error (wrongly)
};
```

The same root cause also prevented the `ALL_REMAINING_HEADERS_ARE_OPTIONAL` builder branch from ever being reached for responses with only optional headers remaining.

<details>
<summary>Original Prompt</summary>

A route like the following is showing a type error. It should not.

```ts
export const DELETE: deleteOrder = ($) => {
  const deleted = $.context.deleteOrder($.path.orderId);
  if (!deleted) {
    return $.response[404];
  }
  return $.response[200];
};
```

</details>

## Manual acceptance tests

- [ ] A route handler that returns `$.response[200]` with no body in the spec compiles without type errors
- [ ] A route handler that returns `$.response[404]` with no body in the spec compiles without type errors
- [ ] Routes with a body (`$.response[200].json(data)`) continue to work unchanged
- [ ] `ResponseBuilderFactory` with no-body status codes: the factory value is directly assignable to `COUNTERFACT_RESPONSE` without calling any builder method
- [ ] A response with only optional headers (no content) resolves to the `ALL_REMAINING_HEADERS_ARE_OPTIONAL` builder, exposing `.header()` and `.ALL_REMAINING_HEADERS_ARE_OPTIONAL`

## Tasks

- Updated `GenericResponseBuilder` in `src/counterfact-types/index.ts` to use `Omit<Response, "examples">` in both `OmitValueWhenNever` checks, so the always-present `examples: {}` field no longer interferes with completion detection
- Added TSD type tests for no-body response factory assignability to `COUNTERFACT_RESPONSE`
- Added TSD type test verifying that responses with only optional headers correctly resolve to the `ALL_REMAINING_HEADERS_ARE_OPTIONAL` builder
- Added changeset (patch)
